Falsifies `extensible_host_controller_interface::verification::a_producer_ring_stays_in_bounds`.

The defect: `ProducerRing::enqueue` compares the next index with `entries` where it should compare
with `entries - 1`, the link slot. The ring then writes a TRB on the link slot and never emits the
link, so the controller walks off the end of the segment.

Expected to fail: the harness's final `assert!(ring.enqueue < entries - 1)`: the enqueue index is left standing on
the link slot after the last ordinary TRB.

diff --git a/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/ring.rs b/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/ring.rs
--- a/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/ring.rs
+++ b/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/ring.rs
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@
         let placed = trb.with_cycle(self.cycle);
         self.enqueue += 1;
         let mut link = None;
-        if self.enqueue == self.entries - 1 {
+        if self.enqueue == self.entries {
             link = Some((
                 self.enqueue,
                 TransferRequestBlock::link(self.base).with_cycle(self.cycle),
